      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add integrations catalog for agents and editors",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add a first-class Integrations section and catalog for Agent Skills, editors, terminal control surfaces, one-shot harnesses, and the future Station runtime\n- make the default `crabbox init` skill conform to the Agent Skills metadata requirements and test its parsed frontmatter\n- document the thin CLI integration contract, current Zed and Herdr status, MCP non-goals, and the boundary for long-running in-box harnesses\n\n## Why\n\nCrabbox already has several extension surfaces, but they are scattered across `crabbox init`, the Zed package, the Herdr plugin, editor handoff, run evidence, and Station design notes. Calling all of these \"plugins\" would blur distinct trust and lifecycle boundaries.\n\nThis change establishes **Integrations** as the product-level umbrella:\n\n- local agents and IDEs remain thin clients of the installed CLI;\n- one-shot repository harnesses use normal runs or jobs;\n- long-running harness daemons remain future Station workloads.\n\nThe related Agent Skill fix addresses a concrete root cause: the generated `SKILL.md` body was useful, but it omitted the required YAML `name` and `description` frontmatter, so standards-based clients could not reliably recognize it as a valid skill.\n\n## User impact\n\nUsers get one discoverable catalog for the integrations available today, package-only surfaces, and contract-only work. New local integrations have an explicit credential, lifecycle, cancellation, and validation contract. The default generated Agent Skill is now valid without introducing a generic executable plugin loader, MCP server, or model-credential forwarding path.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `go test ./internal/cli -count=1`\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh`\n- generated a temporary repository with the built CLI and validated `.agents/skills/crabbox/SKILL.md` with the Agent Skill validator\n\nThe docs gate also exercised all 10 Zed tasks through the Crabbox CLI boundary and rebuilt the documentation site navigation.\n",
