        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add SSH lease copy and tunnels",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- preserve provider-native copy backends and add a resolved SSH/rsync fallback for both `crabbox cp` directions\n- add `crabbox tunnel` with loopback-only local forwarding, accepting-listener readiness, and owned process-tree teardown\n- keep resolved credentials and proxy policy in private temporary OpenSSH configs, including SSH-config aliases, proxy routes, WSL2, and native Windows handling\n- document the command and feature surfaces; thank `@onmax` in the changelog\n\nCloses https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/1067\nCloses https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/1068\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go build ./... && go vet ./... && go test ./internal/cli/... -run 'Cp|Copy|Tunnel|SSH' -count=1`\n- Windows compile-only test for `./internal/cli`\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh`\n- `scripts/live-ssh-localhost-smoke.sh` (`cp` round trip, tunnel readiness, process cleanup)\n- source-blind behavior validation against an isolated binary\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base origin/main` — clean\n\n## Notes\n\n- native provider copy remains preferred when available\n- SSH fallback requires local rsync 3.4.3 or newer; native Windows SSH targets remain on provider-native copy, while WSL2 targets are supported\n- tunnel binds both local and remote forward endpoints to `127.0.0.1` and prints an HTTP URL after readiness\n",
